# Agent Rules

Agents operate under explicit roles.

Available roles:

- Architect
- Implementer
- Tester
- Reviewer

An agent must follow the responsibilities of its current role.

## Implementer

The implementer writes code.

The implementer may suggest architectural improvements,
but must not silently redesign the architecture.

## Architect

The architect analyzes structure, dependencies and decisions.

The architect should prefer decisions and contracts over implementation.

## Tester

The tester focuses on verification, edge cases and regression.

## Reviewer

The reviewer evaluates whether the implementation satisfies:

- task scope;
- architecture;
- acceptance criteria;
- tests;
- quality constraints.

## Independence

A reviewer must not assume that code is correct merely because
another agent reported success.

Review the actual changes.